                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="147" value="npm &lt;strong data-end=&quot;142&quot; data-start=&quot;129&quot;&gt;before v3&lt;/strong&gt; (nested dependencies): -&amp;nbsp;Before npm v3, dependencies were nested exactly according to the dependency graph.&lt;div&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-end=&quot;722&quot; data-start=&quot;698&quot; data-section-id=&quot;qex817&quot;&gt;Problems with npm v2&lt;span class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchor&quot; aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;ul data-end=&quot;863&quot; data-start=&quot;724&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;li data-end=&quot;753&quot; data-start=&quot;724&quot; data-section-id=&quot;u4mn2t&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Lots of duplicate packages.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;li data-end=&quot;785&quot; data-start=&quot;754&quot; data-section-id=&quot;13nfye4&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Deeply nested &lt;code data-end=&quot;784&quot; data-start=&quot;770&quot;&gt;node_modules&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;li data-end=&quot;863&quot; data-start=&quot;786&quot; data-section-id=&quot;a876bw&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Windows often hit the &lt;code data-end=&quot;820&quot; data-start=&quot;810&quot;&gt;MAX_PATH&lt;/code&gt; limit because paths became extremely long.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1000" y="-970" width="680" height="310" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="148" value="" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1880" y="-1030" width="335" height="136.26" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="243" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="149" target="241">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="149" value="&amp;nbsp;npm v3+ (flattened): -&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Starting with npm v3, npm tried to &lt;strong data-end=&quot;941&quot; data-start=&quot;932&quot;&gt;hoist&lt;/strong&gt; as many dependencies as possible to the top level node_modules folder.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;This solved the deep nesting problem, but introduced the &lt;strong data-end=&quot;1168&quot; data-start=&quot;1146&quot;&gt;phantom dependency&lt;/strong&gt; problem because your app could now accidentally access &lt;code data-end=&quot;1236&quot; data-start=&quot;1224&quot;&gt;picocolors&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: initial; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(255, 255, 255), rgb(0, 102, 102));&quot;&gt;Phantom dependency mean that package was installed by the some other dependency package of our project, but because now after the npm v3 onward, all the packages are installed on the top level node_modules folder, we can also directly use that dependency installed package, without the name of that package in dependency in our project package.json&lt;br&gt;So now the problem will arise when we willl uninstall our project dependency package, now becuase we using this dependency installed package in our project, we will get package not found error, becuase this dependency installed package was also uninstalled with our project dependency package&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1140" y="-601.8699999999999" width="566" height="206.87" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
